Rune Bastion engine patch: compile only the shader variants that are actually drawn with.

Godot 4.7.2's GLES3 driver, the first time a shader is bound, compiles every variant of it
(colour, colour+instancing, depth, depth+instancing for scene shaders) with the default
specialization, then compiles the specialization the draw needs. On desktop these land in the
shader cache; the web has no shader cache, so they are compiled on every visit, and a scene
shader is never drawn with the default specialization (draws always set the lightmap, light and
fog bits). Measured in the warm-up of level 2 (tools/perf/shader_compiles.sh): 80 of 159 programs
and 74% of the compile time were these unused programs. With this patch each specialization is
compiled on first use only. Web only (WEB_ENABLED) and only without a shader cache.

diff --git a/drivers/gles3/shader_gles3.cpp b/drivers/gles3/shader_gles3.cpp
index 4fe333e..c3eeca6 100644
--- a/drivers/gles3/shader_gles3.cpp
+++ b/drivers/gles3/shader_gles3.cpp
@@ -709,6 +709,16 @@ void ShaderGLES3::_initialize_version(Version *p_version) {
 	p_version->variants.reserve(variant_count);
 	for (int i = 0; i < variant_count; i++) {
 		p_version->variants.push_back(AHashMap<uint64_t, Version::Specialization>());
+#ifdef WEB_ENABLED
+		// Rune Bastion (tools/engine/patches): with no shader cache (always the case on the web),
+		// compiling every variant with the default specialization here only costs time - scene
+		// shaders are never drawn with it (real draws always set lightmap/light/fog bits) and most
+		// variants of the others are never used. _version_bind_shader() compiles each
+		// specialization that is actually drawn with, on first use.
+		if (!use_cache) {
+			continue;
+		}
+#endif
 		Version::Specialization spec;
 		_compile_specialization(spec, i, p_version, specialization_default_mask);
 		p_version->variants[i].insert(specialization_default_mask, spec);
